3c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:690/362;\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/5/8/581af892e88b9b7e17a19773730e5d9907c03cec_2_690x362.png\" class=\"thumbnail\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"1C1A14\" width=\"690\" height=\"362\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eAI Coding Agent for Building Ambitious Software | Cursor\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003eBuilt to make you extraordinarily productive, agents turn ideas into code. Accelerate development by handing off tasks to Cursor.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486363-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486363-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T11:42:03.719Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":31,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":156.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171028,"topic_slug":"cant-reach-grok-bot-computer","display_username":"prashant kumar","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://cursor.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"AI Coding Agent for Building Ambitious Software | Cursor","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136807,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/cant-reach-grok-bot-computer/171028/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":487904,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-10T06:43:16.482Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the report and the screenshot. I can see the “Can’t reach your computer” screen mentioning firewall, VPN, proxy, and \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isn’t about a reset or reinstall, which is why those don’t help. The error you’re seeing is a failed DNS lookup for \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e, and that DNS resolve happens on your network or ISP side, not ours. This can happen with some ISPs, including your current one Reliance Jio. Please don’t reset or reinstall again, it won’t help here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTry these in order:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Windows, switch to a public DNS: Settings \u0026gt; Network \u0026amp; internet \u0026gt; Wi-Fi (or Ethernet) \u0026gt; your connection \u0026gt; Hardware properties \u0026gt; DNS server assignment \u0026gt; Edit \u0026gt; Manual \u0026gt; turn on IPv4 \u0026gt; Preferred DNS \u003ccode\u003e1.1.1.1\u003c/code\u003e, Alternate DNS \u003ccode\u003e8.8.8.8\u003c/code\u003e \u0026gt; Save. If you’re on Windows 11, also set DNS over HTTPS to On (automatic template) for both. Then fully quit Grok Bot right click the tray icon \u0026gt; Quit and reopen it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Android: Settings \u0026gt; Network \u0026amp; internet \u0026gt; Private DNS \u0026gt; Private DNS provider hostname \u0026gt; enter \u003ccode\u003eone.one.one.one\u003c/code\u003e \u0026gt; Save, then reopen the Grok Bot app.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf it still won’t connect, open Command Prompt on your PC Windows key, type \u003ccode\u003ecmd\u003c/code\u003e, press Enter, run these three commands, and paste the full output here:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"bash\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-bash\"\u003enslookup test.us8.cursorvm.com\nnslookup test.us8.cursorvm.com 1.1.1.1\nnslookup google.com\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnother quick test is to connect via a hotspot from a different carrier not Jio, like Airtel or Vi. If it works right away there, it’s definitely the network.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne more note in case you’re behind a corporate DNS filter or a custom resolver. Your allowlist needs both patterns \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003e*.*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e hosted computers use nested subdomains, and a single wildcard won’t cover them. This doesn’t matter for most home connections, but if the DNS steps above don’t help, it’s worth checking.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know how it goes.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-10T06:43:16.482Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":171028,"topic_slug":"cant-reach-grok-bot-computer","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit